      "general": {
        "abstract": "The ASCA shelf and tall moorings extend 200 km offshore of Hamburg just south of East London on the East coast of South Africa, along the decending TOPEX/Jason satellite ground track # 96, through the core of the Agulhas Current, with Current- and Pressure-recording Inverted Echo Sounders (CPIES) measurements extending the array to 300 km offshore.  There are  two shelf and seven full-depth tall moorings, interspersed with five  CPIES, measuring pressure, current velocities, temperatures and salinities.",
